.vercel

# local env files — never commit real values
#
# NOTE: `.env.production` is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds only VITE_API_BASE,
# which is a public backend URL, and Vite auto-loads it during `vite build` — so
# committing it means Vercel builds correctly with no dashboard configuration.
# Never put a secret in any VITE_* variable: everything VITE_-prefixed is inlined
# into the browser bundle and is therefore public by definition.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
